Aim

To host a static website using Amazon S3 with public access permissions and custom error handling.

Procedure
Step 1: Create S3 Bucket
Open S3 Dashboard.
Click Create Bucket.
Configure:

Bucket Name:

my-static-site-bucket-123
Select nearest region.
Disable:
Block all public access
Create bucket.
Step 2: Upload Website Files
Open bucket.
Go to:
Objects tab
Upload:
index.html
error.html
Step 3: Enable Static Website Hosting
Open:
Properties tab
Scroll to:
Static Website Hosting
Click Edit.
Enable hosting.
Configure:

Index Document:

index.html

Error Document:

error.html
Save changes.
Step 4: Enable Bucket-Level Public Access
Open:
Permissions → ACL
Edit permissions.
Enable:
Everyone (public access) → Read
Save changes.
Step 5: Enable Object-Level Public Access
For index.html
Open file.
Go to:
Permissions → ACL
Enable:
Everyone → Read
Save.
Repeat for error.html
Open error.html.
Enable public read access.
Step 6: Access Website
Open:
Properties → Static Website Hosting
Copy Bucket Website Endpoint.
Open URL in browser.
Step 7: Test Error Page

Open invalid URL:

http://bucket-name.s3-website-region.amazonaws.com/invalid.html
Verify custom error page loads.
Observation
Static website hosting enabled successfully.
HTML files uploaded and publicly accessible.
Website loaded through S3 endpoint.
Custom error page displayed for invalid URLs.
Result

Successfully hosted a static website using Amazon S3 with public access and custom error page support.
